          "email": "caifeng_zhu@163.com",
          "date": "2026-05-13 12:17:52.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-4009 osd-zfs: ordered transaction for zil integration.",
        "message": "LU-4009 osd-zfs: ordered transaction for zil integration.\n\nOrdered transaction is used to satisfy the requirement that when a\ntransaction is committed, all transactions started before it should\nalso be committed.\n\nThere are two aspects of ordered transaction. One is about concurrency\ncontrol and its implementation is osd_tm.c; the other is about log\ncommit and replay and its implementation is osd_zil.c.\n\nThe files that utilize ordered transaction are as follows:\n- osd_handler.c: transaction start and stop are modified here. In\n  osd_trans_start(), transaction id is assigned and the started\n  transaction is put in ordered queue. In osd_trans_stop(), the\n  stopped transaction waits its turn and then triggers log commit\n  and waits commit if it is synchronous.\n\n- osd_object.c, osd_xattri.c and osd_io.c: transaction declaration\n  and execution are modified. In declaration routines, update intent\n  is declared; in execution routines, update intent is acquired and\n  update is packed for logging.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignored\nSigned-off-by: Caifeng Zhu <caifeng_zhu@163.com>\nChange-Id: I54950bf8c6b3e805fcfcde0cda26af4d7aff2017\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
